  "query_preview": "..\n\nTuesday a longwave trough will continue shifting southeast toward\nthe west coast of Canada, carrying a weakening surface low with\nit. Widespread moderate to heavy rain will also break apart from\nnorth to south, leaving a short and welcome break Tuesday.\nUpstream, zonal flow becomes briefly established over the Gulf,\nwith a signal for a shortwave trough digging down from the south-\ncentral coast. These features will carry west-northwest onshore\nflow and some moisture into our area; however, deep moisture will\nlikely shear apart before reaching the Panhandle, limiting heavy\nrainfall potential into mid week. Anticipate low clouds and more \ntypical rainfall, with the farthest reaches of the northern \nPanhandle likely enjoying drier conditions. Near the end of next \nweek ensembles show agreement on a larger system moving into the \nGulf, bringing increased chances for heavier rain and elevated \nsoutheasterly winds along our coast into the weekend.",
